# ONNX Inference with ort

The `ort` crate provides safe, ergonomic Rust bindings to ONNX Runtime, enabling you to run any ONNX model at native speed.

## Setup

```toml
[dependencies]
ort = "2"
ndarray = "0.16"
```

## Loading and Running a Model

```rust
use ort::{Session, Value};
use ndarray::Array2;

fn main() -> ort::Result<()> {
    let session = Session::builder()?
        .with_model_from_file("model.onnx")?;

    let input = Array2::<f32>::zeros((1, 784));
    let outputs = session.run(
        ort::inputs![input.view()]?
    )?;

    let predictions = outputs[0].extract_tensor::<f32>()?;
    println!("Prediction: {:?}", predictions.view());
    Ok(())
}
```

## Performance Tips

- Use `CUDAExecutionProvider` for GPU acceleration
- Batch inputs for throughput
- Profile with ONNX Runtime's built-in tracing

## Use Cases

- Image classification and object detection
- NLP and text embedding
- Real-time audio processing
